
Create a classic rock album cover featuring three vehicles in space, and have the moon in the top right corner. The first car is a red sports car, the second is a green muscle car, and the third is a blue pickup truck. The different colors on subjects that are all vehicles will simultaneously create unity and variety through use of similar subject material and complimentary color. They should all leave light trails of their respective color that trail off into the background and towards the moon. The title of the album is called “Space Race”, and should be in the top left. This will create a sense of rhythm that takes the viewer’s eye from the cars to the title, and then to the moon and then back to the cars. The colors of the moon, the album title, and each vehicle should be bright enough to make them stand out from the darkness of space. This puts emphasis on the respective subjects and will make the viewer feel excited to listen to the hypothetical album. Blur the light trails to give a sense of motion.
